{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Discover optimal autoregressive, integrated, and moving average orders across ((p, d, q) \\times (P, D, Q)_s) grids using parallel Swift Concurrency."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Concurrent Order Selection with AutoARIMA","modules":[{"name":"SwiftForecast"}]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Manually diagnosing autocorrelation functions (ACF) and partial autocorrelation functions (PACF) to select ARIMA orders is time-consuming and error-prone. Standard automated packages like R’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forecast::auto.arima"},{"text":" or Python’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pmdarima"},{"text":" search across candidate orders sequentially.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AutoARIMA"},{"text":" evaluates the entire hyperparameter lattice simultaneously across all CPU cores on Apple Silicon using structured Swift Concurrency (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withThrowingTaskGroup"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Grid Search Architecture","type":"heading","anchor":"Grid-Search-Architecture","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["           Observed Time Series [y_1, y_2, ..., y_N]","                               │","       ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐","       ▼                       ▼                       ▼","ARIMA(1, 1, 0)          ARIMA(2, 1, 1)          ARIMA(0, 1, 2)","Task 1                  Task 2                  Task 3","   │                       │                       │","   ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen      ├─ Hannan-Rissanen","   └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC      └─ Compute AIC\/BIC","       │                       │                       │","       └───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┘","                               ▼","                withThrowingTaskGroup Collector","                               │","                               ▼","                 Sorted Leaderboard & Best Model"],"syntax":null},{"anchor":"Information-Criteria","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Information Criteria"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"AIC (Akaike Information Criterion)","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Penalizes model complexity while rewarding likelihood:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"$$\\text{AIC} = 2k - 2\\ln(L)$$","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"BIC (Bayesian Information Criterion)"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Imposes a stronger penalty proportional to sample size:","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{BIC} = k\\ln(N) - 2\\ln(L)$$"}]}]}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example Usage","anchor":"Example-Usage"},{"code":["import SwiftForecast","","\/\/ 1. Initialize AutoARIMA with bounded search ranges","let autoArima = AutoARIMA(","    maxP: 3,","    maxD: 2,","    maxQ: 3,","    criterion: .aic",")","","\/\/ 2. Concurrently fit candidates across all cores","let result = try await autoArima.fit(series: historicalPrices)","print(\"Optimal Order: \\(autoArima.bestOrder!) with AIC: \\(autoArima.bestScore!)\")","","\/\/ 3. Generate multi-step forecasts","let forecast = try await autoArima.forecast(horizon: 12)","print(\"Forecasted points: \\(forecast.forecast.predictions)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Stability & Convergence Guarantees","type":"heading","anchor":"Stability--Convergence-Guarantees","level":2},{"text":"Zero-Variance Degenerate Inputs","type":"heading","anchor":"Zero-Variance-Degenerate-Inputs","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If an input series is constant or exhibits zero numerical variance ($\\text{var} < 10^{-12}$), standard likelihood optimization can diverge or enter infinite loops. ","type":"text"},{"code":"AutoARIMA","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" detects zero variance upfront, immediately fitting an exact ARIMA(0, 0, 0) constant model:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoids matrix singularities in the Hannan-Rissanen and Yule-Walker algorithms.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Guarantees instant return without stalling the task group.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Fixed-Iteration-Bound","text":"Fixed Iteration Bound"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All internal parameter search loops are strictly bounded by a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations = 500"},{"text":" ceiling, ensuring that optimization cannot exceed the configured iteration bound in deterministic time across parallel worker threads.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAParallel","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaparallel"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Automated Time Series","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMACriterion"],"anchor":"Automated-Time-Series"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/SmoothingAndDecomposition","doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/KoopmanOperator"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMA":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarima","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMA","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMA"}],"type":"topic","title":"AutoARIMA","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AutoARIMA"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Automated hyperparameter grid search for ARIMA and SARIMA time-series models."}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/ArimaAndSarima":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/arimaandsarima","role":"article","title":"ARIMA & SARIMA Time Series Models","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Forecast univariate time series using Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (ARIMA) and Seasonal ARIMA (SARIMA).","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/ArimaAndSarima"},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/AutoARIMAOrder":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/autoarimaorder","role":"symbol","title":"AutoARIMAOrder","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A structure identifying the selected ARIMA \/ SARIMA order.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftForecast\/documentation\/SwiftForecast\/AutoARIMAOrder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AutoARIMAOrder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftForecast/documentation/SwiftForecast/SmoothingAndDecomposition":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftforecast\/smoothinganddecomposition","role":"article","title":"Time Series Forecasting, Smoothing & Kalman Filtering","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Model trends, seasona